&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Money math in floating point is fine for a display estimate, but for anything transactional use integer minor units.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Formatting and RTL tips
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intl.NumberFormat handles currency symbols and digits per locale. Try "ar-SA" or "ur-PK" with a matching currency such as SAR or PKR.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set dir="auto" on text blocks so mixed Urdu/English content lays out correctly, or set dir="rtl" on the root when the whole UI is RTL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use CSS logical properties (margin-inline-start instead of margin-left) so one stylesheet works in both directions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The API returns translations per language, so pass the lang parameter that matches your UI locale and read the matching key from the translations object.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Going further
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Zakat is tied to a lunar year, so pairing the calculator with dates is natural. The &lt;a href="https://quranicapi.online/api/hijri-calendar" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Hijri Calendar API&lt;/a&gt; can help you build a reminder widget; check its page for the response shape. You can browse everything on the &lt;a href="https://quranicapi.online/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;QuraniAPI home page&lt;/a&gt;, and the open repository is at &lt;a href="https://github.com/sunnahsourceofficial-droid/sunnahsource-islamic-api" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;sunnahsource-islamic-api on GitHub&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Wrap-up
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We built a small component with a live, cached and bundled-sample data path, a simple 2.5% calculation using the API's rate, and locale-aware formatting. Next ideas: store the user's inputs locally, add a language switcher backed by the lang parameter, and show the guideline items text from the API under the result. Again, this is software only; please consult a scholar for your own zakat.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Short answer:&lt;/strong&gt; a React or Vite app sends an empty &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;div id="root"&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; and builds the page in the browser. AI crawlers don't run that JavaScript, so to ChatGPT, Claude and Perplexity your site has no text. Pre-render it: build the HTML of each route at deploy time with a 15-line script, and React takes over in the browser as usual. You don't need to rewrite anything in Next.js.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When I audited 286 developer portfolios for &lt;a href="https://wickz.dev/en/blog/portfolios-invisible-to-ai/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;an earlier study&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;98 of them (34%) showed fewer than 20 words&lt;/strong&gt; to a bot that doesn't run JavaScript. Most were React, Vue or Vite single-page apps. They look great to a person and blank to a crawler.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Check your site in 10 seconds
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ask for your page the way a crawler does and search for your main heading:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;curl -s -A &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"GPTBot/1.1"&lt;/span&gt; https://yourdomain.com/ &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; grep -i &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"your main heading"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;If nothing prints, AI crawlers can't see that text. You can also open &lt;code&gt;view-source:https://yourdomain.com&lt;/code&gt; in the browser. If the body is a lone &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;div id="root"&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, that's what the bots get.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The fix: 4 small changes
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Vite can build your app twice: once for the browser and once for Node. The Node build can turn a route into an HTML string, and a short script saves one file per route. I tested this with Vite 8, React 19 and React Router 8.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Add a placeholder in &lt;code&gt;index.html&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight html"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"root"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;&amp;lt;!--app--&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Create &lt;code&gt;src/entry-server.jsx&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, which renders a route to a string:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;renderToString&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"react-dom/server"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StaticRouter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"react-router"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"./App.jsx"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;render&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;renderToString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;StaticRouter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;location&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;StaticRouter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. In &lt;code&gt;src/main.jsx&lt;/code&gt;, change &lt;code&gt;createRoot&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;hydrateRoot&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, so React reuses the HTML that's already there instead of building it from scratch:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;hydrateRoot&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"react-dom/client"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;BrowserRouter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"react-router"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"./App.jsx"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;hydrateRoot&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getElementById&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"root"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;BrowserRouter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;BrowserRouter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Add &lt;code&gt;prerender.js&lt;/code&gt; at the project root&lt;/strong&gt; and list your public routes:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fs&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"node:fs"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;render&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"./dist-ssr/entry-server.js"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;routes&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/projects"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/about"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;template&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;readFileSync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"dist/index.html"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"utf8"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;routes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;template&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;replace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&amp;lt;!--app--&amp;gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;render&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;file&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`dist${url === "/" ? "" : url}/index.html`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;fs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;mkdirSync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;file&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;replace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/index.html"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;recursive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;fs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;writeFileSync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;file&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then point the build script in &lt;code&gt;package.json&lt;/code&gt; at the three steps:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"build"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"vite build &amp;amp;&amp;amp; vite build --ssr src/entry-server.jsx --outDir dist-ssr &amp;amp;&amp;amp; node prerender.js"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Run the build and &lt;code&gt;dist/projects/index.html&lt;/code&gt; now has your real heading, text and links. Run the &lt;code&gt;curl&lt;/code&gt; again after you deploy and you should see it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Things that break (and how to fix them)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;window&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt; at the top of a component.&lt;/strong&gt; The Node build doesn't have them. Move that code into a &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt;, which only runs in the browser.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Different output in Node and in the browser.&lt;/strong&gt; If something like &lt;code&gt;Date.now()&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;Math.random()&lt;/code&gt; changes what's rendered, React warns about a hydration mismatch. Render the same thing in both places, and update it in a &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Routes with parameters.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;/blog/:slug&lt;/code&gt; isn't a list the script can guess. Build the list from your data (the same JSON or Markdown files your app reads) and add those URLs to &lt;code&gt;routes&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;title&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; Every page still has the title from &lt;code&gt;index.html&lt;/code&gt;. If you want one per route, replace it in the same loop, with a &lt;code&gt;.replace()&lt;/code&gt; on the &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;title&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; tag.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Testing locally.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;vite preview&lt;/code&gt; returns the home page for &lt;code&gt;/projects&lt;/code&gt; and the right file for &lt;code&gt;/projects/&lt;/code&gt;. Static hosts like Vercel and Netlify serve &lt;code&gt;dist/projects/index.html&lt;/code&gt; for &lt;code&gt;/projects&lt;/code&gt; before applying the SPA rewrite, so it works when deployed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  When this isn't the right fix
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If your content changes per visitor or every few minutes (a dashboard, prices in real time), pre-rendering at deploy time won't keep up. That's a job for server-side rendering, and at that point a framework like Next.js or React Router's framework mode is worth it. For a portfolio, a landing page or a small business site, pre-rendering is enough.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Don't want to touch your build?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If your site is a React or Vite SPA and you'd rather not deal with it, &lt;a href="https://wickz.dev/en/services/full-stack-web-development/?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_campaign=prerender-react-vite" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;I can do it for you&lt;/a&gt;. I pre-render your public pages, check that AI crawlers can read them, and leave your app working exactly as it does now.&lt;/p&gt;

